course: dictionary
lesson: 8236
title: Words in a story: revolver
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A revolver is a small gun. Its round part turns, and it holds several bullets. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it, because they are its context and often give clues. In «detectives waving revolvers», the word waving tells you the detectives hold the revolvers up, as a weapon in a chase.
explain: Look at the other things in the list: «warders waving halberds» and «policemen waving truncheons». Halberds and truncheons are tools or weapons, so the list is about people who carry weapons. Revolver fits that group, so you can guess it is a weapon too. Always check your guess by putting it into the sentence.
explain: Real guns are very dangerous. Stories can show them safely on the page, but in real life you must never touch one. If you ever see a gun, do not touch it, move away quietly and tell an adult straight away.
fact: A revolver is a small gun, also called a pistol.
fact: The cylinder of a revolver turns, and it holds several bullets.
fact: «Detectives waving revolvers» means detectives holding small guns up during a chase.
fact: «Truncheon» means a police club, and «halberd» means a long pole with an axe-blade.
fact: Real guns are dangerous. If you see one, do not touch it, move away and tell an adult.
exercise: «The detectives in the chase were waving revolvers.» What is a revolver? | *A small gun that holds several bullets | A long pole with an axe-blade | A round hat for men | A police club
exercise: «Policemen waving truncheons» is in the same list as revolvers. What is a truncheon? | *A police club | A small gun | A pot of soup | A bowler hat
exercise: You see a real gun lying on the ground. What should you do? | Wave it around to look brave | *Do not touch it, move away and tell an adult | Pick it up to see how heavy it is | Hide it under your coat
test: «Men like ancient warders, waving halberds» is a clue. What is a halberd? | A type of bowler hat | *A long pole with an axe-blade | A soft toy | A small gun
test: What do the words «waving» and «detectives» suggest about a revolver? | *It is held up as a weapon during a chase | It is a sweet to eat | It is a kind of bird | It is a dish for dinner
exam: The list says «warders waving halberds, policemen waving truncheons and detectives waving revolvers», so what is a revolver? | A walking-stick for old men | A police club for stopping crowds | A kind of bowler hat | *A small gun with a turning cylinder for several bullets
